{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1482","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1482","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1482\",\"parent_revision\":\"3f2fa7aa8005bdbf3bd0da450538318509a584efa608841327c718541047b181\",\"root_revision\":\"3f2fa7aa8005bdbf3bd0da450538318509a584efa608841327c718541047b181\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo data-handling defects in the SAM MCP server:\\n\\n**Defect 1 \u2014 `artifact_read` silent first-entry selection:**\\n`artifact_read` uses `entries[0]` with no selection logic. `get_by_type` returns entries in insertion order (not recency order despite the comment saying \\\"most recent\\\"). When multiple agents register artifacts of the same type, callers receive the first-registered entry with no warning that others were skipped.\\n\\n**Confirmed location:** `backlog_core/server.py` lines 2383\u20132390. The comment \\\"Use the first (most recent) entry\\\" is factually wrong \u2014 order is insertion order only (`artifact_registry.py` line 294: plain list comprehension).\\n\\n**Defect 2 \u2014 `set_fields_json` double serialization:**\\n`sam_update`'s `set_fields_json` parameter is typed `str | None`. MCP callers must serialize a dict to a JSON string before passing it \u2014 the tool then deserializes it internally. FastMCP supports `dict` parameters natively.\\n\\n**Confirmed location:** `sam_schema/server.py` lines 521\u2013569. Zero test coverage for `set_fields_json` in any test file.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect (\u00d72) \u2014 incorrect selection logic; incorrect type annotation\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 lines 2383\u20132390 (artifact_read entry selection)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 lines 521\u2013569 (set_fields_json type and deserialization)\\n\\n**Tests (new):**\\n- `tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py` \u2014 multi-entry artifact_read test\\n- `tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 set_fields_json dict parameter test\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Defect 1:**\\n- All callers of `artifact_read` when >1 entry of same type exists\\n- `skills/start-task/SKILL.md`, `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md`, `skills/context-integration/SKILL.md`, `skills/final-verification/SKILL.md`\\n- `tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py` \u2014 all tests use single-entry fixture (no coverage of multi-entry path)\\n\\n**Defect 2:**\\n- All `sam_update` callers using `set_fields_json`\\n- `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 documents `sam_update` without noting serialization requirement\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P1** \u2014 Defect 1 is silent data loss in a documented multi-agent scenario. Defect 2 causes agent call failures when passing dicts directly.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Defect 1 \u2014 `artifact_read`:**\\n- [ ] When multiple entries exist for a type, returns most recently registered entry (sort by `created_at` desc)\\n- [ ] Response includes `warnings` listing count and paths of skipped entries\\n- [ ] Single-entry behavior unchanged\\n- [ ] Comment \\\"Use the first (most recent) entry\\\" replaced with accurate documentation\\n- [ ] New test: register two entries of same type; verify most recent returned AND response includes warning with skipped entry paths\\n\\n**Defect 2 \u2014 `set_fields_json`:**\\n- [ ] Parameter type changed from `str | None` to `dict[str, Any] | None`\\n- [ ] Internal `json.loads` deserialization removed; parameter used directly as dict\\n- [ ] Docstring no longer describes it as a \\\"JSON string\\\"\\n- [ ] New test: call `sam_update` with `set_fields_json={\\\"reason\\\": \\\"test\\\"}` (native dict); verify field updated\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**S (small)** \u2014 ~1\u20132 hours including tests. Both fixes are localized to single functions. No model changes needed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Defect 1:**\\n1. Register two `task-plan` artifacts for the same issue at different paths\\n2. Call `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"task-plan\\\")`\\n3. Observe: first-registered entry returned, second silently ignored, no warning in response\\n\\n**Defect 2:**\\n1. Call `sam_update` with `set_fields_json={\\\"reason\\\": \\\"testing\\\"}` (native dict)\\n2. Observe: FastMCP rejects at schema validation \u2014 parameter type is `str`, not `object`\\n3. Workaround required: `set_fields_json='{\\\"reason\\\": \\\"testing\\\"}'` (pre-serialized string)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using SAM MCP tools**, I want **`artifact_read` to return the correct entry when multiple exist** and **`set_fields_json` to accept a native dict instead of requiring double serialization** so that **data is not silently lost and agents don't need to pre-serialize parameters**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research finding \u2014 mcp-ux-improvements-20260404.md, validated mcp-ux-improvements-validation-20260404.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Defect 1 (5-Whys):**\\n1. `artifact_read` uses `entries[0]` with no selection mechanism\\n2. `get_by_type` returns insertion-order list, not sorted by `created_at`\\n3. `ArtifactEntry.created_at` field exists but `get_by_type` ignores it\\n4. Single-artifact-per-type assumption \u2014 multi-agent scenarios were not designed for\\n5. All `artifact_read` test fixtures use single-entry setup \u2014 multi-entry path never tested\\n\\n**Defect 2 (5-Whys):**\\n1. Callers must pre-serialize dict to JSON string before passing `set_fields_json`\\n2. Parameter type annotation is `str | None` \u2014 FastMCP generates a string schema\\n3. `str` was likely a workaround for early MCP type limitations; FastMCP now supports `dict` natively\\n4. Internal `json.loads` is the symptom; the type annotation is the cause\\n5. Zero test coverage for `set_fields_json` \u2014 latent ergonomics bug not caught\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Defect 1 \u2014 `artifact_read` fix:**\\n\\n```python\\n# Sort by created_at desc; fall back to insertion order for entries without timestamp\\nentries_sorted = sorted(entries, key=lambda e: e.created_at or \\\"\\\", reverse=True)\\nentry = entries_sorted[0]\\nif len(entries_sorted) > 1:\\n    skipped = [e.path for e in entries_sorted[1:]]\\n    out.warnings.append(\\n        f\\\"Multiple {artifact_type!r} artifacts found ({len(entries_sorted)}); \\\"\\n        f\\\"returning most recent ({entry.path}). Skipped: {skipped}\\\"\\n    )\\n```\\n\\nAlternative: add `path: str | None = None` parameter to `artifact_read` for direct path selection.\\n\\n**Defect 2 \u2014 `set_fields_json` fix:**\\n\\n```python\\nset_fields_json: Annotated[\\n    dict[str, Any] | None,\\n    Field(description=\\\"Field=value pairs to set on the plan or task\\\")\\n] = None,\\n# Remove the json.loads call; use dict directly:\\nif set_fields_json is not None:\\n    set_fields = {str(k): str(v) for k, v in set_fields_json.items()}\\n```\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d0c0ecc9bf5c7468f2f5f7957986fcf8b2723be57704c733e78bc2dbce3eaaa8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCtuXw\"}"}